.TH "EPX\-PRICES" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-prices \- read and change prices
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx prices [flags]
epx prices [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads and changes prices. Without a site, Emporix lists the prices of every site, so list and for\-product require \fB\-\-site\fR and read that site\(aqs prices only; an unknown site lists nothing. create and update change one price, bulk\-create and bulk\-update many, each from \fB\-\-file\fR, and delete deletes one.
.PP
Its reads require different OAuth scopes; the help of each names them. Its writes require the price.price_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx prices bulk\-create"
Create prices in bulk.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx prices bulk\-create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the prices in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON array of prices, each as create takes it.
.PP
Emporix takes up to 200 items in one request (epx refuses more), carries out each on its own and answers with the result of each: when one failed, epx prints the response, lists the items that failed on standard error (one that failed with 500, 502, 503 or 504 may have been carried out all the same) and exits with the code that their failures share (for example 5 for a 409 Conflict, 4 for a 404), else 1.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the price.price_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx prices bulk\-update"
Upsert prices in bulk.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx prices bulk\-update [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the prices in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON array of prices, each with its id, or creates those that do not exist (an upsert). An item that failed with 500 may be one whose metadata.version is stale: Emporix reports it so, not as 409 Conflict. Read it again before you retry it.
.PP
Emporix takes up to 200 items in one request (epx refuses more), carries out each on its own and answers with the result of each: when one failed, epx prints the response, lists the items that failed on standard error (one that failed with 500, 502, 503 or 504 may have been carried out all the same) and exits with the code that their failures share (for example 5 for a 409 Conflict, 4 for a 404), else 1.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the price.price_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx prices create"
Create a price.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx prices create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the price in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON object with at least itemId, currency, location and tierValues: the id of each tier of the price model that priceModelId names, as \fBepx price\-models get ID \-o json\fR prints it, with a priceValue. Without an id, Emporix makes one, which the response gives. Emporix does not refuse an id that a price has already: it stores a second price with it, and each delete of that id removes one. Leave id out, or change a price with update.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the price.price_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx prices delete"
Delete a price.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx prices delete PRICE_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the price PRICE_ID. Emporix answers an unknown PRICE_ID as one that it deleted (204 No Content). PRICE_ID is the ID that \fBepx prices list \-\-site S\fR shows.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type PRICE_ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the price.price_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx prices for\-product"
List the prices of a product on a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx prices for\-product PRODUCT_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads prices. Without a site, Emporix lists the prices of every site, so list and for\-product require \fB\-\-site\fR and read that site\(aqs prices only; an unknown site lists nothing. TIERS lists the value of each price tier as sent; tier quantities and net or gross come from the price model (\fBepx price\-models get\fR with the priceModelId of \fB\-o json\fR). Customer and price\-list restrictions and sale prices are only in \fB\-o json\fR. PRODUCT_ID is the product id (as in \fBepx products list\fR), not its code. An unknown id lists nothing.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, ITEM, TYPE, CURRENCY, COUNTRY, SITES, TIERS, FROM, TO.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx prices get"
Show one price.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx prices get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads prices. Without a site, Emporix lists the prices of every site, so list and for\-product require \fB\-\-site\fR and read that site\(aqs prices only; an unknown site lists nothing. TIERS lists the value of each price tier as sent; tier quantities and net or gross come from the price model (\fBepx price\-models get\fR with the priceModelId of \fB\-o json\fR). Customer and price\-list restrictions and sale prices are only in \fB\-o json\fR.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, ITEM, TYPE, CURRENCY, COUNTRY, SITES, TIERS, FROM, TO.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx prices list"
List the prices of a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx prices list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads prices. Without a site, Emporix lists the prices of every site, so list and for\-product require \fB\-\-site\fR and read that site\(aqs prices only; an unknown site lists nothing. TIERS lists the value of each price tier as sent; tier quantities and net or gross come from the price model (\fBepx price\-models get\fR with the priceModelId of \fB\-o json\fR). Customer and price\-list restrictions and sale prices are only in \fB\-o json\fR.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, ITEM, TYPE, CURRENCY, COUNTRY, SITES, TIERS, FROM, TO.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx prices match"
Match the best price of products.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx prices match [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Matches the price of one unit of each product that \fB\-\-product\fR names (the product id as in \fBepx products list\fR) that Emporix would charge on the site \fB\-\-site\fR names, for the country \fB\-\-country\fR names, in the currency \fB\-\-currency\fR names: of the prices that apply, the lowest after discounts, converted with the tenant\(aqs exchange rates and tax classes where the price is in another currency or for another country. ID is the matched price (of the price list PRICE LIST, if any), ORIGINAL and EFFECTIVE (discounted) the price of one unit, TOTAL that of QUANTITY, gross where TAX is true. Other quantities and units, a customer or a legal entity go in \fB\-\-body\fR.
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole.
.PP
Requires the price.price_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, ITEM, PRICE LIST, SITE, COUNTRY, QUANTITY, ORIGINAL, EFFECTIVE, TOTAL, TAX.
.TP
\fB\-\-country <code>\fR
The code of the country to match the price for, e.g. NL (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-currency <code>\fR
The code of the currency to match the price in, e.g. EUR (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-product <ID>\fR
A product ID whose price to match (repeatable; required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-site <code>\fR
The code of the site whose price to match (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.SS "epx prices search"
Search the prices of products.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx prices search [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the prices of up to 100 products (\fB\-\-product\fR, the product id as in \fBepx products list\fR), on the site and in the currency that \fB\-\-site\fR and \fB\-\-currency\fR name, else on every site and in every currency, shown as list shows prices; \fB\-o json\fR also lists the products without a price. Other criteria (a customer, a date, net or gross values) go in \fB\-\-body\fR.
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole.
.PP
Requires the price.price_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, ITEM, TYPE, CURRENCY, COUNTRY, SITES, TIERS, FROM, TO.
.TP
\fB\-\-currency <code>\fR
The code of the currency whose prices to read, e.g. EUR.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-product <ID>\fR
A product ID whose prices to read (repeatable, up to 100; required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-site <code>\fR
The code of the site whose prices to read.
.SS "epx prices update"
Upsert a price.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx prices update PRICE_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the price PRICE_ID with the one in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON object as \fBepx prices get PRICE_ID \-o json\fR prints it, or creates it with that id where none exists (an upsert; not with \fB\-\-partial\fR: Emporix answers a missing price with 404 Not Found, exit 4). Send the price\(aqs metadata.version as read to change it only if nobody changed it since: Emporix answers 409 Conflict otherwise. PRICE_ID is the ID that \fBepx prices list \-\-site S\fR shows.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the price.price_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-partial\fR
Change only the fields that the body gives; without it, the body replaces the whole price.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
